  "study_notes": {
    "observed": "Nov 2025 649 Avenue N (same panorama at headings 243 and 246, 17-30 m, behind palms): a plain weathered concrete box about 11 m tall at the NNW end; white sheet-metal ducts bridging at two to three levels with a vertical riser; a tall white cylindrical vessel at the SSE end; a low dark plant enclosure under the ducts; a low dark round tank toward the street.",
    "inferred": "Duct levels, posts, vessel and tank heights, the riser position and louvres are production inference. WSW, SSE and NNW sides are unphotographed: plain walls in the photographed materials with one inferred personnel door on the NNW face of the box. Ducts are elevated slabs on steel posts (walkable underneath).",
    "footprint": "Frozen ring split along the box ENE face frame (edge e70): concrete box, low plant room and duct bridge, two elevated duct runs, the round lobes as a tall vessel and a low tank."
  }
